  {
    "sha": "5516dbc3c86f3af5123b782633bed562dc3a1e09",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVoU8JdoAKDU1MTZkYmMzYzg2ZjNhZjUxMjNiNzgyNjMzYmVkNTYyZGMzYTFlMDk",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T08:46:05Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Mike Kinney",
        "email": "mike.kinney@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-12T08:46:05Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): hold the adaptive planning budget per margin attempt\n\nThe growth planner's running budgets (length, law 2; vertices past a\nlength, law 3) were summed over the margin attempts. A plan whose first\nwall margin ran out a revolution before its fronts were done - a matter\nof nanometres of ring geometry - was made again from a wider margin with\na whole attempt already charged, and refused for it: the rotary r7 bar's\ndeveloped level at radius 5.0 was refused at 22.5 k + 7.6 k tool radii,\nand HSM-planned in 22.3 k with its openings 250 nm deeper.\n\nEach attempt is now counted on its own (Work::attempt, at the top of\nPlanner::grow). The limits and refusal texts are unchanged; every\nrefusal on our fixtures falls inside its first attempt as before. The\nr7 bar's level 5.0 and the rotary window's levels 6.0 and 5.0 are\nHSM-planned, at 0, 8, 16, 62 and 250 nm of perturbation alike (heavy\ntwins in adaptive::budget::twins), and the rotary pins name them.\n\nStacked on PR #1080 (#982). Decision: docs/decisions/1051-planning-budget-edge.md\n\nFixes #1051\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
      "tree": {
        "sha": "d5a5fe4090c396e9e6aa9cb937fef3282e269721",
        "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/trees/d5a5fe4090c396e9e6aa9cb937fef3282e269721"
      },
      "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/NeoTech/Camcraft/git/commits/5516dbc3c86f3af5123b782633bed562dc3a1e09",
      "comment_count": 0,
      "verification": {
        "verified": false,
        "reason": "unsigned",
